{"lines": ["On the twelfth of September, 1952, at about seven fifteen in the evening, two brothers, Edward and Fred May, and their friend Tommy Hyer saw a bright object cross the sky over Flatwoods, West Virginia. They said it came down on a nearby farm.", "They ran to get others. A group climbed the hill, among them Kathleen May, Neil Nunley, Ronnie Shaver, and a West Virginia National Guardsman, Eugene Lemon.", "Nunley reported a red, pulsating light. Lemon raised a flashlight, and for a moment he saw a tall figure, a round red face inside a pointed, hood-like shape.", "Lemon reportedly screamed and dropped the flashlight. The whole group ran.", "Later accounts get bigger. The writer Gray Barker, in Fate magazine in January 1953, described a ten foot figure, a blood-red face, and a head like the ace of spades.", "Afterward, some of the boys reported a pungent mist, nausea, and swollen throats. A doctor found no cause.", "Here is the problem. Every retelling added something, and the arms, the height, the shape all changed with the teller.", "Rule one. Write down what you saw, in your own words, before anyone asks you a question. Once somebody else's version is in your head, it is hard to get yours back."], "words": [["On", 0.0, 0.12], ["the", 0.12, 0.2], ["twelfth", 0.2, 0.62], ["of", 0.62, 0.67], ["September,", 0.67, 1.14], ["1952,", 1.48, 2.34], ["at", 2.48, 3.08], ["about", 3.08, 3.26], ["seven", 3.26, 3.72], ["fifteen", 3.72, 4.18], ["in", 4.18, 4.48], ["the", 4.48, 4.58], ["evening,", 4.58, 4.92], ["two", 5.28, 5.4], ["brothers,", 5.4, 5.8], ["Edward", 6.14, 6.26], ["and", 6.26, 6.66], ["Fred", 6.66, 6.88], ["May,", 6.88, 7.12], ["and", 7.12, 7.44], ["their", 7.44, 7.58], ["friend", 7.58, 7.8], ["Tommy", 7.8, 8.22], ["Hyer", 8.22, 8.64], ["saw", 8.64, 8.98], ["a", 8.98, 9.1], ["bright", 9.1, 9.34], ["object", 9.34, 9.78], ["cross", 9.78, 10.24], ["the", 10.24, 10.6], ["sky", 10.6, 10.84], ["over", 10.84, 11.24], ["Flatwoods,", 11.24, 11.92], ["West", 11.92, 12